evidence[1]{path,hash,excerpt,truncated}:
  ".project/done-work.md#upstream-project-drift","sha256:08d7b0acc1d4582304dd87c26ced444e32933c28e5822504323c2dcff727b1d6","## upstream-project-drift — shipped 2026-10-16\n\nImprovements made in three downstream projects (climbing-lab-monorepo, LAH, RN) were classified and the portable ones taken into the base as release 2.23.0 (2026-10-16, big-batch, commit `58cfd7f`). S0 produced a drift ledger of 178 rows (D3/D4: most climbing docs and rules are project adaptations, and 47 RN rows are `node → bun` text only; real RN improvements are ten rows: the Orca start hooks, `stuck-uphill-detector`, `pre-ship-verify`, the `hooks.json` path fix and the `skill-defaults.test.mts` `IN_BUNDLE_REPO` guard). S1 rules plus the graphify dangling-edge finish; S2 runtime child ownership taken from climbing after three fixes (D7); S3 Orca minimum version 1.4.224 with a strict `isSupportedVersion` (x.y.z, at most six digits per part) wired into preflight, launch gate and the start worker check, pulled forward (D6); S4/S5 task ownership, with apply, admit and grader taken from climbing (D9); S6 hooks hardening; S7 doctor, validator and skill tests; S8 `workflow/` and `templates/` hunks (13 files); S10 added (D8) so `opencode-service.mts free` stops a stale `opencode serve --service` and `orca-run dispatch` calls it before the first live OpenCode attempt; S9 version 2.23.0, GAUNTLET node 1327/0 and bun 1323/0, Linux Docker runtime 69/0, and a sync proof inside the ledger (131/178 rows match, the rest explained). Pitch no-gos held: no config-format change (that became `unified-toon-config`), no version-range parser (`orca-engines-range`), no role pools (`orca-role-pools`), no edits inside LAH, RN or climbing (read-only sources), and no wholesale copy of a project file over the base without a ledger row and reason; the standing workflow-tooling no-gos applied. Projects were not synced: `git status --porcelain` and HEADs `02a2f91`, `48a721d`, `bfb81b6` identical before and after.\n\nRabbit holes resolved: two `isSupportedVersion` grammars (LAH loose, climbing strict) → strict now, later replaced by `orca-engines-rang",true
